sessions.summary:
The game is finished. `npm test` passes (18 of 18) and `npm run build` succeeds; its only warning is that the bundle is over 500 kB. I have not run `npm run dev` in a browser, because only those two commands are allowed here. Gameplay, pointer lock and the no-console-errors requirement were checked by reading the code only.

**What I found:** earlier sessions had already written the whole engine and the full UI (menu, chunk streaming, sky, mining, building, inventory and crafting, pause, F3 debug, saving). I read every engine module against the spec and every game and UI file, and found no contract violations.

**What I changed:**
- **`noise.js` / `world.js`:** I halved the noise's internal frequency and adjusted the terrain scales to match. Before, the "points 0.01 apart differ by less than 0.05" rule held in practice but was not guaranteed in the worst case; now it is, and the terrain looks the same.
- **New `src/engine/contract.test.js`:** 7 extra tests that `node --test` picks up automatically. They cover:
  - noise continuity over 20,000 point pairs;
  - terrain generation on 75 chunks, including negative coordinates (column layers, coal and iron height limits, at least one coal per chunk, tree position and trunk height);
  - removing an edit when a block is reverted, exact save output, save/load round trip, and the version and y-range errors;
  - face culling between glass and other blocks and across chunk borders;
  - raycast with an unnormalized direction, skipping water, and starting inside a block;
  - physics: jumping a 1-block step but not 2, sneak stopping at an edge, a 1-second step landing exactly on the floor, and not changing the input player;
  - edge cases in inventory, crafting, mining and the day/night cycle.

  Two of my own test cases were wrong at first; I fixed the tests, not the engine.
- **`input.js` / `Game.js`:** three small fixes:
  - Esc now opens the pause menu even when the mouse isn't locked.
  - Holding Esc no longer closes the inventory and then pauses straight away.
  - If the mouse lock arrives late while the inventory is open, the game no longer switches back to play with the inventory still open.

The game's title is "Cubária" and all textures are drawn in code.
